  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Humanitarian assistance to protect migrant women and those with diverse sexual o</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Expected Result/target 1. 3,000 migrant women, those with diverse sexual orientations and gender identities, and their families, who want to settle permanently, as well as host communities, will benefit from increased access to sexual, reproductive and menstrual healthcare via the Mobile Tent2 where they will be able to receive medical, legal and psychological assistance to exercise their rights.  Expected Result/target 2. 1,500 migrant women &quot;walkers&quot; and those accompanying them will increase their protection mechanisms through access to information, guidance, hygiene materials (including menstrual management), unconditional cash transfers, as well as humanitarian transport.  Expected Result/target 3. 500 local, community and institutional stakeholders in Arauca and the main destinations for migrant populations coming into Colombia from Venezuela will strengthen their capacities to minimise protection risks, facilitate integration and promote the coexistence of migrant women, those with diverse sexual orientations and gender identities and those accompanying them in transit, who want to settle permanently, and their host communities.</narrative>
  </description>
